cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the iLang loader, please cite it as below."
title: "iLang loader: the official iLang runtime for any model"
abstract: >-
  The iLang loader fetches the official iLang runtime from the canon
  repository, verifies its sha256, keeps a Last Known Good copy on disk and
  adds it as the first system message of any model's conversation without
  changing the user's messages. It is model-agnostic, has no dependencies,
  checks for a new runtime at most once an hour, fails open when nothing
  verified is available unless strict mode is set, and can pin an exact
  runtime version so that benchmarks, audits and papers can be re-run against
  the same context. Python and JavaScript implementations are provided.
type: software
